  "prefLabel": "Cor 101.24 Quarantine",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cor 101.24 “Quarantine” means the initial arrival process during which the newly arrived person under departmental control is tested, medically evaluated, orientated, and generally prepared for confinement or treatment in a secure environment.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Cor 100) #7446, eff 2-6-01; ss by #12500, eff 3-23-18 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Cor 100)",
